WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.733
<v Odhran Okonjo>Hello both, thanks for basically, jumping on. So, I've got news on Willowmere Cottage.

00:00:06.933 --> 00:00:09.933
<v Wilhelmina Okonjo>Oh God, okay, is it good news?

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:12.400
<v Cormac Haverstock>Let him talk, love.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.867
<v Odhran Okonjo>Ha. It's mixed. So the vendors have come uh, back on your offer.

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:19.467
<v Cormac Haverstock>Right.

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:25.733
<v Odhran Okonjo>You offered $850. They've said they'd accept, um, a bit more. They want 45k.

00:00:25.933 --> 00:00:29.400
<v Wilhelmina Okonjo>That's, what, like four percent more?

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.467
<v Cormac Haverstock>Bit under. Three and a half.

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:42.733
<v Odhran Okonjo>About that, yes. And, between us, I think they'll go lower, they're going through a divorce and they need it sold before the court date.

00:00:42.933 --> 00:00:47.933
<v Cormac Haverstock>Ah. That's, um. That's useful to know. Bit grim, but useful.

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:50.200
<v Odhran Okonjo>I didn't say it.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.800
<v Wilhelmina Okonjo>Say what? I mean, Ha.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.067
<v Odhran Okonjo>Ha. basically, Exactly. So, how are you both feeling about the house itself?

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:07.267
<v Wilhelmina Okonjo>I love it. I love it. The garden, sort of, the little shed, the view over I mean, to the Malvern Hills...

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:10.400
<v Cormac Haverstock>The survey's what worries me.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:18.867
<v Odhran Okonjo>Yes. So the surveyor flagged some damp in the back bedroom, and the roof's, um, got maybe ten um, years left.

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:21.733
<v Cormac Haverstock>And the subsidence thing.

00:01:21.933 --> 00:01:27.933
<v Odhran Okonjo>Historic. Historic subsidence. It's been basically, monitored, it's stable.

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:33.200
<v Wilhelmina Okonjo>What does that mean sort of, for, basically, like, insurance?

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:43.667
<v Odhran Okonjo>Premiums um, can be a bit higher. Maybe fifteen to twenty percent above normal. Hartfield Mutual are usually decent for that sort of thing.

00:01:43.867 --> 00:01:49.867
<v Cormac Haverstock>Okay. And the mortgage? We're with Kingsmead Building Society in principle.

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:53.333
<v Odhran Okonjo>What like, rate did they give you?

00:01:53.533 --> 00:01:56.133
<v Cormac Haverstock>14.5% fixed, five years.

00:01:56.333 --> 00:02:03.533
<v Odhran Okonjo>That's good. That's really good, actually. I've seen people at five and a quarter this month.

00:02:03.733 --> 00:02:07.400
<v Wilhelmina Okonjo>We put down ten percent. Is that enough?

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:13.067
<v Odhran Okonjo>For that rate, yes. More is sort of, always better, but ten's fine.

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:25.000
<v Cormac Haverstock>We were going to put down more, but my company's just announced a restructure and I don't know yet whether I've got a job in January, so we're keeping some back.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.133
<v Odhran Okonjo>Very sensible.

00:02:27.333 --> 00:02:33.600
<v Wilhelmina Okonjo>We're also, um, selling the place in Fenmoor Crossing. My flat. Well, our flat.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:36.667
<v Odhran Okonjo>Oh, right, how's that going?

00:02:36.867 --> 00:02:44.400
<v Wilhelmina Okonjo>Slowly. The buyer's mortgage fell through because apparently he lied about his income, which, wow.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.267
<v Odhran Okonjo>Oof. That happens more than you'd think.

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:52.000
<v Cormac Haverstock>Can I ask about the area? The schools?

00:02:52.200 --> 00:03:00.133
<v Odhran Okonjo>Sure. Primary's rated outstanding, in the village. Secondary is the one in Ashcombe Vale, which is fine.

00:03:00.333 --> 00:03:02.000
<v Wilhelmina Okonjo>And crime?

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:08.467
<v Odhran Okonjo>Very low. The only thing anyone sort of, complains about is the bypass traffic.

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:13.000
<v Cormac Haverstock>And there's no plans to build on the field behind?

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:23.333
<v Odhran Okonjo>Not that I know of. I'd check with the council though, between us the farmer who owns it has been quietly talking to a housing developer.

00:03:23.533 --> 00:03:25.600
<v Wilhelmina Okonjo>Ooh. Neighbours!

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.000
<v Cormac Haverstock>Not helpful, love.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:33.467
<v Odhran Okonjo>Ha. So, what would you like me to basically, say to the vendors?

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:38.733
<v Cormac Haverstock>Let's say $1,900, and we can complete by the end of February.

00:03:38.933 --> 00:03:44.067
<v Wilhelmina Okonjo>Can we say mid-February? I want to be like, in by Valentine's.

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:47.467
<v Cormac Haverstock>That's sort of, not how it works.

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:56.467
<v Odhran Okonjo>Ha. basically, I'll say end of February, with flexibility. And I'll push the damp I mean, as a reason for the number.

00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:58.000
<v Cormac Haverstock>Good.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:04.067
<v Odhran Okonjo>Can I um, just get your solicitor's you know, details again for the memo?

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:13.600
<v Cormac Haverstock>Yes, it's Penrose Fairclough, um, and the contact is Ambrose Pennyworth-Hale. Her email is jem.ravensworth@gildersleeve.test.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:17.667
<v Odhran Okonjo>Lovely. And best basically, number for you?

00:04:17.867 --> 00:04:19.467
<v Cormac Haverstock>555-0119.

00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:23.333
<v Wilhelmina Okonjo>Or mine, I always pick up! 570-555-0197.

00:04:23.533 --> 00:04:30.667
<v Odhran Okonjo>Ha, um, noted. like, Okay, I'll um, come back to you by tomorrow afternoon. Fingers crossed.

00:04:30.867 --> 00:04:33.000
<v Wilhelmina Okonjo>Fingers and toes!

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:35.000
<v Cormac Haverstock>Thanks. Bye.
